+// joe Linux: <pwd.h> and <grp.h> read /etc/passwd and /etc/group, in the
+// format every Linux system uses, and nothing else. Android's fixed and
+// per-app accounts (AID_*, u0_a123) and its partitions' account files are
+// gone. Lines that are empty, comments, or NIS markers (+ and -) are skipped,
+// as are lines without the right number of fields.
